# Derived finding corpora — BUILD-LOCAL WORKING DATA, regenerated by scripts/build_rip_corpus.py and
# scripts/fetch_fix_regions.py from DISCLOSURES.json + upstream diffs. Not committed because it is
# derived and machine-specific, not because of any embargo: what ships from this work is the
# generalized rule set in rules/. Those rules' ground-truth comments cite ONLY publicly-disclosed
# findings (crate/file/line of any unfiled finding is kept out — see the 2026-08-03 sweep). The DVRA
# corpus stays tracked — that target is deliberately vulnerable and published as such.
/corpus/rip-findings.jsonl
/corpus/fix-regions.jsonl

# advisory-db paired corpus (W33/E7) — 4.4 GB of upstream crate sources at two versions each, plus
# the per-cell scoring output. Rebuilt from scratch by scripts/harvest_advisory_db.py; the tracked
# artifact is the SCORE in docs/sast-experiments.md, not the trees it was computed over.
/corpus/tp/
/corpus/tn/
/corpus/e7-cells.jsonl
/corpus/e7b-fixsites.jsonl
/corpus/advisory-manifest.jsonl

# private submission-planning queue — names unfixed findings, never commit
